<script>
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { groupByCause, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';
  import Callout from '#lib/kb/Callout.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';

  const repo = 'https://github.com/kamyk-pl/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues';

  // The desk's own grouping (causes.ts), with the one-day moves it noted taken out of the cause
  // they were filed under: they are not a swap, so they are a problem of their own.
  const merged = uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471);
  const moved = merged.filter((r) => notes.oneDayMove.includes(r.id));
  const groups = groupByCause(merged.filter((r) => !notes.oneDayMove.includes(r.id)), tenantOf);
  const count = (cause) => groups.find((g) => g.cause === cause)?.reports.length ?? 0;
  const problems = [
    { cause: 'parser', what: 'day and month swapped by the shared parser', n: count('parser'), ticket: 1 },
    { cause: 'hint', what: 'booking-v3 form hints MM/DD to day-first tenants', n: count('hint'), ticket: 2 },
    { cause: 'one-day move', what: 'date moves by one day, as across time zones', n: moved.length, ticket: 4 },
  ];
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its {merged.length} reports hold three
problems. Each has its own ticket now, and the fix queued for #4471 closes only the first.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Fixing the parser leaves the booking-v3 hint and the one-day moves open.
</Callout>

## The split

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>problem</th><th>reports</th><th>ticket</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    {#each problems as p (p.cause)}
      <tr>
        <td><code>{p.cause}</code>: {p.what}</td>
        <td>{p.n}</td>
        <td><a href="{repo}/{p.ticket}">#{p.ticket}</a></td>
      </tr>
    {/each}
  </tbody>
</table>

`parser` and `hint` are the desk's causes from `causes.ts`, placed by tenant and channel. The
one-day moves are the reports the desk noted in `desk-notes.json`. #4471's own table files them
under `parser` by tenant, but day and month do not swap in them, so they are counted here once,
as their own problem.

## The three problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day
  first, so day and month swap: booked 7 April, invite for 4 July. Channels: app and email,
  and the form on booking-v2. Fix: parse in the tenant's locale.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field for tenants who
  write the day first. People type what the hint says, the form reads it the tenant's way, so
  the date swaps. The parser fix does not touch this path. Fix: the hint follows the tenant's
  locale, as booking-v2's does.
- **one-day move**: no swap. The date moves by one day: the invite says Tuesday, the calendar
  says Monday; a client in Lisbon and one in Toronto got different days for one meeting. Fix:
  not known yet; check how invites store and convert times.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line, and none of
the subjects names a cause. Intake's tag guesses from the reporter's browser, not the tenant,
so it does not split them either.

